      "math_academy_id": "q-35202",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14210035/assets/46022df1ffb1b45ffe344658075dd363f3e2856798050fdbe85aacff0bc98ebe.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y={f}^{-1}(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ is a reflection of $y=f(x)$ in the line $y=x.$ Of the given options, the only graph satisfying this condition is the one shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14210035/assets/53ba6c80f60bdf35052e0bc018317f741d4ddd781ed9156f915df91b855a93f7.png)\n\nNotice that the points on $y=f(x)$ have corresponding points on $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ with the coordinates swapped.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0,1) & ⟶(1,0) \\\\ (-2,3) & ⟶(3,-2) \\\\ (-3,5) & ⟶(5,-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
